{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts@L101","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":101,"end":107}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":101,"end":107},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:638d51211bf71b55baedc49137567d7612ee5d8c86ae213052fc0f158655a012","meta":{"text":"The schema-valid, secret-safe content hash for a file given its classification + text.\n- normal file → full content hash (unchanged behavior).\n- sensitive `properties` → key-only hash (keys sorted; values never hashed).\n- any other sensitive file (binary store / secret resource) → path-only hash (bytes never hashed).\nNon-Mule files (no classification) always get the full content hash."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts@L20","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":20,"end":21}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":20,"end":21},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:25d92c6f6f487ffdf897f8846a19a15b5823a2bc82f572a4ab5adaf35f56a97b","meta":{"text":"True if a path is worth reading text from for Mule dialect detection. Descriptors carry the\ndialect signal (packaging, mule-artifact.json); a config peek confirms legacy namespaces."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts@L44","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":44,"end":49}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":44,"end":49},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2f94f37a2c81cb5be8331e483f052ae553cb82b1eed880c0ea919b48e65699fe","meta":{"text":"Read text for marker-bearing files, classify Mule projects, and stamp a clone-safe\n{@link FileClassification} + role-specific `lang` onto each Mule FileMeta IN PLACE. Non-Mule files\nare untouched. Returns Mule diagnostics for the parse-phase aggregator (Task 7). Mutates only the\nFileMeta objects passed in; deterministic; pure over the read text."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts@L71","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":71,"end":75}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":71,"end":75},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:043d9692844bf9254062b6f61005ae0ba9ab923cae9163e28d722bc86b8f4709","meta":{"text":"Extract property KEYS from a `.properties`/`.yaml`/`.yml` text — names only, NEVER values. Used to\nfingerprint sensitive config files for change detection without persisting any secret bytes.\nRecognizes `key=value` and `key: value` (any indentation), ignoring `#`/`!` comments and blanks."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts@L87","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":87,"end":89}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":87,"end":89},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:703de64721f5d2e983ef4bc5ab4ef50227173aae6f3339f990098144f9e5991f","meta":{"text":"`blake3:<hex>` over the SORTED property keys of a sensitive config file — stable across value\nedits and reordering, and never includes a secret value. Empty key set hashes the empty string\n(still a valid `blake3:` digest) so a file that is all-comments still gets a stable redacted hash."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts@L94","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":94,"end":96}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/discover.ts","span":{"start":94,"end":96},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:7de94686ec02c70dbcb89c4f6bc51dadc24fb62c9b3784f7d1376f646f896ad9","meta":{"text":"`blake3:<hex>` over the repo-relative path only — for sensitive binary files (keystores,\ntruststores, .jks/.p12) where there are no keys to extract and the bytes are secret. The hash\nstays a valid `blake3:` digest (schema requires it) while never touching file content."}}
